<caml:Content xmlns:caml="http://lc.ca.gov/legalservices/schemas/caml.1#"><p>Qualification of a motor club for a certificate of authority under this part does not require prior qualification with the Secretary of State under the Corporations Code for an intrastate business, but the issuance to it of a certificate of authority under this part does not relieve such foreign applicant of any duty to qualify with the Secretary of State pursuant to the Corporations Code before transacting intrastate business in this state.</p></caml:Content>